%% alt: A redirect. The browser asks the app server for a short code. The app checks the cache; on a hit it has the long URL; on a miss it reads a replica, falling back to the primary for a just-created link, then fills the cache. It sends a click event to the queue without waiting, and answers with a 302 redirect.
%% caption: The only work on the critical path is a cache lookup. The click event is sent without waiting for it.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as Browser
  participant A as App server
  participant C as Cache
  participant R as Replica
  participant Q as Click queue
  B->>A: GET /aZ3kP9q
  A->>C: get aZ3kP9q
  alt hit
    C-->>A: long URL
  else miss
    A->>R: read (primary if brand new)
    A->>C: set with TTL
  end
  A-)Q: click event, no wait
  A-->>B: 302 to the long URL
